[W-NO-VALUES] Warning: `Loop` has no values: every constructor needs a value of `Loop` first
    ╭─[ soundness/proof-irrelevance-14-expose-loop.sw:15:6 ]
    │
 15 │ type Loop: Prop =
    │      ──┬─  
    │        ╰─── this type can never be built
 16 │   | MkLoop (next: Loop)
    │                   ──┬─  
    │                     ╰─── a `Loop` is needed here
    │ 
    │ Note: a value is built from finitely many constructors, so a type whose every constructor holds one of itself is empty. Give a constructor without that field (an end case, as `Nil` is for a list), or, for an endless stream, a function from the position: `Nat -> a`
